d":"2026-11-23T12:14:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50545207/2026-college-football-power-rankings-top-25-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tennessee fined by SEC after fans throw golf balls on field","description":"Tennessee was fined $250,000 by the SEC after fans threw golf balls and mustard bottles onto the football field late during Saturday's win over LSU.","published":"2026-11-23T01:42:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50568028/tennessee-fined-sec-fans-throw-golf-balls-field","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Notre Dame loses safety Luke Talich to torn Achilles","description":"Notre Dame starting safety Luke Talich sustained a torn right Achilles tendon in Saturday's win against SMU, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-22T23:15:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50566676/notre-dame-loses-safety-luke-talich-torn-achilles","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What Week 12's unexpected results mean for Rivalry Week and beyond","description":"After another chaotic weekend, we look at the playoff and conference races on the line with one game to go.","published":"2026-11-22T23:54:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50563018/week-12-results-rivalry-week","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 recruit AJ Randle Jr. flips from Miami to Notre Dame","description":"Notre Dame coach Marcus Freeman flipped Miami pledge AJ Randle Jr., ESPN's No. 9 outside linebacker in the 2027 recruiting class, to fill a late-cycle need.","published":"2026-11-22T22:48:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50565158/2027-recruit-aj-randle-jr-flips-miami-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pac-12 reveals unique flex schedule for season's final week","description":"The Pac-12 announced its unique flex schedule for the final week of the regular season early Sunday morning.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564960/pac-12-reveals-unique-flex-schedule-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Montana State ranked No. 1, 5-7 LIU makes FCS bracket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-23T00:02:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest rewards DC Scottie Hazelton with contract extension","description":"Wake Forest defensive coordinator Scottie Hazelton has signed a contract extension.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564902/wake-forest-rewards-dc-scottie-hazelton-extension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5031157/reed-harris","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_Harris_(American_football)"},"pick":{"pick":49,"round":2,"team":"LAR","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Reed Harris (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_Harris_(American_football)","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:14Z","intro":"Reed Harris is an American football wide receiver for the Arizona State Sun Devils. He previously played for the Boston College Eagles.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Harris was born in Minnesota, and moved to Conrad, Montana when he was a year old, growing up on a 12,000 acre farm. Harris moved to Great Falls, Montana when he was in 8th grade, later attending Great Falls High School where he was the football team's starting quarterback as a sophomore and junior. He moved to wide receiver during his senior season and finished with 553 yards and three touchdowns. Harris finished his high school career completing 229 passes for 21 touchdowns, while adding 1,575 yards and 13 touchdowns on the ground, with 36 receptions for 536 yards and four touchdowns through the air. He also added 83 tackles with ten being for a loss, nine sacks, five fumble recoveries, and a forced fumble on defense. Coming out of high school, Harris was rated as a three-star recruit in football, basketball, and track by 247Sports, and was ranked as the top player in the state of Montana in the class of 2023. He committed to play college football for the Boston College Eagles over offers from other schools such as Iowa State, Oregon State, Montana, Montana State, Colorado State, Utah State, San Diego State, Central Michigan, Harvard, Idaho, and Idaho State."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"BOSTON COLLEGE\nAs a freshman in 2023, Harris appeared in four games, making one catch, as he was redshirted. In week 2 of the 2024 season, he caught his first career touchdown in a win over Duquesne. During the 2024 season, Harris played in all 13 games with 11 starts, catching 17 passes for 486 yards and four touchdowns. During the 2025 season, he totaled 39 catches for 673 yards and five touchdowns; after the conclusion of the season, he entered the NCAA transfer portal."}]}}